    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39426" root="نجز" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَجْزٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نُجْزٌ</span></b>  are syn. You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنْتَ عَلَى</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَجْزِ حَاجَتِكَ</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَاجَتِكَ</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نُجْزِ</span></b> , <i>Thou art on the
point of accomplishing thy want.</i> (S, K.)

